      "handover": {
        "evidence": [
          {
            "id": "e1",
            "quote": "Nvidia $NVDA is in talks to provide a roughly $250 billion financial backstop for OpenAI as part of a massive data center project in southern Ohio, according to The Wall Street Journal .",
            "one_line": "Quartz于2026-07-27转述《华尔街日报》称，Nvidia正洽谈为OpenAI俄亥俄州数据中心项目提供约2500亿美元融资担保。",
            "speaker": "Quartz（转述《华尔街日报》）",
            "original_who": "The Wall Street Journal",
            "original_day": "",
            "tier": "传闻",
            "event_time": "2026-07-27",
            "links": [
              "c1"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "e3",
            "quote": "The project is sited on a decommissioned uranium-enrichment facility roughly 50 miles south of Columbus, and the full cost — including chips — could exceed $500 billion, making it the largest data center project announced to date.",
            "one_line": "Quartz于2026-07-27报道，俄亥俄州项目包含芯片的总成本可能超过5000亿美元。",
            "speaker": "Quartz",
            "original_who": "",
            "original_day": "",
            "tier": "第三方看法",
            "event_time": "2026-07-27",
            "links": [
              "c3"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "e4",
            "quote": "In a parallel negotiation, Nvidia is also in talks to help fund OpenAI's acquisition of chips, a figure the Journal said could reach $350 billion.",
